---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { coreOrderPolicy } from '../../core-order-policy.mjs';
import { site } from "../../data.mjs";
import { orderTerms } from "../../ordering.mjs";
const path = "/guides/compare-custom-mailer-quotes/";
const title = "How to Compare Custom Mailer and Garment Bag Quotes";
const schema = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "Article", headline: title, author: { "@id": `${site.origin}/#organization` }, publisher: { "@id": `${site.origin}/#organization` }, mainEntityOfPage: `${site.origin}${path}`, dateModified: "2026-11-08", inLanguage: "en" };
const breadcrumbs = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", itemListElement: [{ "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: site.origin }, { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Buying Guides", item: `${site.origin}/guides/` }, { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Compare quotes", item: `${site.origin}${path}` }] };
const fields = [
  ["Mailer type and construction", "Are the offered structures the same?"],
  ["Outer and usable dimensions", "Are units, flap allowance and measurement directions clear?"],
  ["Material and thickness", "What exactly is included in the measurement?"],
  ["Artwork and print sides", "Are colors, coverage, placement and printing method included?"],
  ["Quantity per size/design", "Is the quantity breakdown by size, color and artwork agreed?"],
  ["Sample route", "Stock sample, artwork proof or custom printed sample?"],
  ["Production start milestone", "Which approvals or payments start the schedule?"],
  ["Delivery scope", "Which destination, service and charges are included?"],
  ["Currency and validity", "Which currency, validity period and pending items apply?"]
];
---
<Layout title="Compare Custom Mailer & Garment Bag Quotes | Welltroy" description="Compare mailer and garment zipper bag quotes by specification, quantity, samples and delivery. Download a worksheet for inner bags and outer shipping packs." canonicalPath={path} schemas={[schema, breadcrumbs]}>
  <section class="page-hero approval-guide-hero"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/guides/">Buying Guides</a> / Compare quotes</div><p class="eyebrow">After you receive quotations</p><h1>{title}</h1><p class="lead">Compare custom mailer and garment bag quotes against one written specification. Check that usable size, material, print coverage and delivery scope match, then compare the complete quoted cost and any unresolved conditions.</p><p class="muted">By Welltroy · Updated <time datetime="2026-11-08">8 November 2026</time></p><nav class="anchor-links" aria-label="In this guide"><a href="#worksheet">Comparison worksheet</a><a href="#garment-quotes">Garment bags &amp; outer mailers</a><a href="#costs">Cost items</a><a href="#bubble-delivery">Bubble delivery comparison</a><a href="#timing">Timing</a><a href="#approval">Final approval</a></nav></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container article-layout"><article class="article-main">
    <p>This guide covers custom poly and bubble mailers and garment zipper inner bags. Compare each construction separately: a plain shipping bag, a bubble-lined mailer and a garment inner bag have different roles, even when their outside dimensions look similar. For an apparel order, use the <a href="#garment-quotes">inner-bag and outer-mailer comparison</a>.</p>
    <h2>What Should I Include When Requesting a Custom Shipping Bag Quote?</h2>
    <p>Identify the exact mailer format and state whether your dimensions are outer or usable inner dimensions. Include the packed product, quantity per size and design, artwork, intended finish, sample needs and destination. Use consistent units and mark requirements that are still open.</p>
    <p>The <a href="/guides/custom-packaging-500-pieces/#poly-cost">poly mailer cost and MOQ guide</a> helps you prepare an itemized initial enquiry and confirm the order breakdown. This comparison worksheet is for the next step: checking whether the replies describe the same order.</p>
    <p>For an initial itemized request, add quantities to compare and your destination postal code in the product brief: <a href="/products/poly-mailers/#quote-delivery-checks">poly mailers</a>, <a href="/products/poly-bubble-mailers/#quote-delivery-checks">poly bubble mailers</a>, <a href="/products/metallic-bubble-mailers/#quote-delivery-checks">metallic and holographic bubble mailers</a>, or <a href="/products/zipper-bags/#quote-delivery-checks">garment zipper bags</a>. Keep each requested quantity tied to the same size, material and artwork.</p>
    <h2 id="worksheet">What Should I Compare in Packaging Quotes Before Price?</h2>
    <p>Copy the written terms from each quotation into this worksheet. “To confirm” marks an unanswered field; it is not a supplier offer or a price estimate.</p>
    <p class="table-scroll-hint">Swipe the table horizontally to see Quote B and the questions.</p><div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Custom mailer quotation comparison worksheet"><table><caption class="sr-only">Blank worksheet for comparing two custom mailer quotations</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Field</th><th scope="col">Quote A</th><th scope="col">Quote B</th><th scope="col">Question to resolve</th></tr></thead><tbody>{fields.map(([field, question]) => <tr><th scope="row">{field}</th><td>To confirm</td><td>To confirm</td><td>{question}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
    <p>For a bubble mailer, confirm usable inner space after accounting for the lining. For a printed poly mailer, confirm print sides and the offered method. For a metallic mailer, identify the exact surface effect. Compare the <a href="/products/poly-mailers/#mailer-comparison">three mailer formats</a> if the construction is still undecided.</p>
    <h2 id="garment-quotes">How Do I Compare Frosted or Clear Garment Bag Quotes?</h2>
    <p><strong>Compare the same garment-bag version: usable space below the zipper, offered material and thickness convention, finish, closure, artwork and pieces per version.</strong> Keep the chosen inner bag separate from any outer shipping mailer. A frosted or clear appearance alone does not identify the material, film gauge or zipper construction.</p>
    <div class="garment-quote-layers"><article><p class="eyebrow">Inner packaging</p><h3>Garment Zipper Bag</h3><ul><li>Folded garment group and inserts</li><li>Usable width and height below the zipper</li><li>PE/PVC preference or the material actually offered</li><li>Frosted/clear reference, closure and artwork</li><li>Pieces and sample reference for this bag version</li></ul></article><article><p class="eyebrow">Separate shipping layer</p><h3>Outer Mailer, if Needed</h3><ul><li>Dimensions of the closed inner pack</li><li>Inner packs per customer-order combination</li><li>Outer construction, usable space and closure</li><li>Outer artwork and packing reference</li><li>Its own required pieces and quoted amount</li></ul></article></div>
    <h3>Check These Differences Before Comparing Prices</h3>
    <dl class="garment-quote-checks"><div><dt>Material, usable size and closure</dt><dd>Copy what each supplier actually offers, including the film measurement convention, usable opening and zipper. Keep an unanswered detail pending instead of treating two similar photographs as the same specification.</dd></div><div><dt>Finish, logo and garment identification</dt><dd>Match the physical finish reference, artwork revision, print sides and intended label position. State any visibility or barcode-reading check needed for the actual garment. Ask for a revised offer when a different material or finish is proposed.</dd></div><div><dt>Quantity by product and bag version</dt><dd>{coreOrderPolicy.summary} {coreOrderPolicy.breakdown} An inner bag and an outer mailer are separate products: a combined quantity does not establish the minimum for either, and one inner bag does not necessarily mean one outer mailer per order.</dd></div><div><dt>Sample and production references</dt><dd>Identify what the stock sample, digital proof or custom sample represents, plus unresolved changes. Keep the quote with the <a href="/guides/custom-mailer-sample-approval/#garment-sample-trial">garment sample checks</a> and the approved garment-to-bag mapping.</dd></div></dl>
    <h3>How Should I Compare an Inner-and-Outer Packaging Quote?</h3>
    <p>List each product amount separately, then identify setup, samples, packing and delivery items. If one charge covers both products, state its scope and count it once. Compare the same destination, ZIP/postal code, delivery point, currency and quotation validity. Keep excluded, estimated and unknown charges visible; a combined order total is not the unit price of one component bag.</p>
    <p>Use the <a href="/guides/apparel-inner-bags-and-shipping-mailers/#sku-record">garment and outer-pack version record</a> to keep the same packing combinations in both replies. For a requested material or inspection record, clarify the scope through the <a href="/materials-and-documents/?product=zipper-bags#document-request-builder">garment document request</a>.</p>
    <div class="guide-callout garment-quote-download" id="garment-quote-record"><h3>Record Written Replies for the Same Apparel Pack</h3><p>The blank TXT worksheet separates inner and outer specifications, pieces, sample references, charges and open questions. Copy its reply block for each supplier or quantity option. You can attach a completed TXT record to the enquiry form, subject to its current file limits.</p><a class="button button-secondary" href="/downloads/garment-inner-outer-quote-comparison.txt" download>Download Garment Quote Comparison (TXT)</a></div>
    <div class="button-row garment-quote-actions"><a class="button" href="/quote/?product=zipper-bags#quote-form" data-quote-placement="content">Request Garment Bags Only</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/quote/?product=multiple-products#quote-form" data-quote-placement="content">Request Inner Bags and Outer Mailers</a></div>
    <h2 id="costs">Separate the Cost Items</h2>
    <ul><li><strong>Products:</strong> unit price, quantity per size/design, currency and the total product amount.</li><li><strong>Setup:</strong> any separately quoted artwork, plate or tooling charges, and whether they apply again on a repeat order.</li><li><strong>Samples:</strong> the sample type, any quoted preparation charge and the courier arrangement.</li><li><strong>Packing and delivery:</strong> carton requirements, freight, destination and other stated charges.</li><li><strong>Unresolved items:</strong> identify charges still awaiting confirmation before comparing totals.</li></ul>
    <div class="guide-callout"><strong>Build a total for the same scope:</strong> add the quoted product amount and the applicable, confirmed additional items. Keep each currency separate until you agree on a comparison basis. Mark an unknown charge as pending; ask for an updated quotation when its amount is known.</div>
    <p>If destinations or delivery terms differ, resolve those differences first. Ask which freight and destination charges are included, excluded or estimated. Keep the quoted terms beside your comparison so the total can be checked.</p>
    <h2 id="bubble-delivery">How Do I Compare Bulk Delivery Costs for Bubble Mailers?</h2>
    <p><strong>Compare the same bags, quantity, packing and destination before dividing the total by the number of bags.</strong> A price for a carton, a price per bag and a freight estimate use different units. Ask the supplier to identify each basis in writing.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Bubble mailer carton and delivery cost checks"><table><caption>Resolve the scope before calculating a comparable cost per bag</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Quote detail</th><th scope="col">What to confirm</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Sale unit</th><td>Price per bag or carton, pieces per carton, carton count and the total confirmed bag quantity.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Packing basis</th><td>Proposed carton dimensions and weights, units and any special labeling or packing request.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Cost scope</th><td>Product, printing/setup, samples/courier, bulk freight and other stated charges; identify what is included or separate.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Destination</th><td>The same country, postal code and delivery point, with destination charges marked included, excluded, estimated or pending.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Comparison basis</th><td>One confirmed specification and quantity, one currency and a clearly stated quotation validity period.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <div class="quote-scope-formula"><strong>When the scope is confirmed</strong><p>Comparable cost per bag = confirmed total for that scope ÷ confirmed number of bags.</p><span>Keep different currencies separate. If a charge is unknown, mark it pending; a provisional total is not a final delivered cost.</span></div>
    <p>Compare quantity tiers separately: a lower unit bag price at a larger quantity does not settle its complete order cost or the storage you need. Keep the supplier's quoted carton plan with each quantity. These are comparison fields, not published Welltroy carton specifications or shipping prices.</p>
    <p>Bulk delivery of empty bags to your business is also separate from the postage for each filled parcel you send to your customers. Follow the chosen carrier/service's measurement rules for those filled shipments.</p>
    <div class="button-row"><a class="button button-secondary" href="/downloads/bubble-mailer-quote-comparison.txt" download>Download a Blank Quote Comparison</a><a class="text-link" href="/products/poly-bubble-mailers/#quote-delivery-checks">Build a Poly Bubble Delivery Brief →</a></div>
    <p>For finish choices and a new request, use the <a href="/guides/metallic-vs-holographic-bubble-mailers/#delivered-quote">bubble mailer quantity and delivery checklist</a>. Before approving the order, keep this comparison with the <a href="/guides/custom-mailer-sample-approval/#bubble-sample-trial">bubble mailer sample checks</a>.</p>
    <h2 id="timing">Compare Timing by Milestone</h2>
    <p>Keep design, sample preparation, sample transit, production and bulk transit as separate stages. Record the event that starts each stage. An estimate measured from artwork approval has a different starting point from one measured from payment or dispatch.</p>
    <p>{orderTerms.design} {orderTerms.sample}</p><p><strong>Bulk production:</strong> {orderTerms.production}</p>
    <p>Confirm your required arrival date and destination with the supplier. See <a href="/ordering/">samples, payment and delivery terms</a> for the current Welltroy process.</p>
    <h2 id="approval">Resolve Exceptions Before Approval</h2>
    <p>Ask for a revised written quotation when you change size, artwork, material, quantity or delivery scope. Keep the final specification, <a href="/guides/custom-mailer-sample-approval/">sample approval record</a> and quotation together, with a version and date for each.</p>
    <p>{coreOrderPolicy.summary} {coreOrderPolicy.breakdown} To request a comparison-ready proposal, send the same specification and destination through our enquiry form.</p><a class="button" href="/quote/?product=multiple-products#quote-form" data-quote-placement="content">Request a detailed quotation</a>
  </article><aside class="side-card"><p class="eyebrow">Related checklists</p><h2>From Brief to Approval</h2><div class="guide-options"><a href="/guides/custom-packaging-500-pieces/"><strong>Prepare your enquiry</strong><span>Write a specification for an initial quote</span></a><a href="/guides/custom-mailer-sample-approval/"><strong>Approve the sample</strong><span>Check mailer or garment bag fit, artwork and the retained reference</span></a><a href="/guides/choose-a-mailer/"><strong>Choose a mailer</strong><span>Compare flexible and cushioned formats</span></a></div><a class="text-link" href="/guides/">All buying guides →</a></aside></div></section>
</Layout>
<style>.approval-guide-hero{padding-block:52px 44px}.approval-guide-hero h1{font-size:clamp(2.15rem,4.3vw,3.5rem);line-height:1.16;text-wrap:balance;max-width:1000px}.article-main h2{font-size:clamp(1.65rem,2.8vw,2.1rem);line-height:1.25;text-wrap:balance}.article-main h3{line-height:1.3;margin-top:28px}.side-card h2{font-size:1.5rem;line-height:1.25}.quote-scope-formula{margin:26px 0;padding:24px;background:var(--cream);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px}.quote-scope-formula strong{color:var(--orange)}.quote-scope-formula p{font-weight:650;line-height:1.6}.quote-scope-formula span{font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.65;color:var(--muted)}@media(max-width:600px){.approval-guide-hero{padding-block:34px 30px}.article-main .button{white-space:normal;text-align:center}}.garment-quote-layers{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:18px;margin:24px 0}.garment-quote-layers article{padding:22px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;background:white;min-width:0}.garment-quote-layers h3{margin-top:8px}.garment-quote-layers ul{padding-left:20px}.garment-quote-checks>div{padding:16px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.garment-quote-checks dt{font-weight:750;color:var(--ink);margin-bottom:8px}.garment-quote-checks dd{margin:0;line-height:1.75}.garment-quote-download{scroll-margin-top:110px}.garment-quote-download h3{margin-top:0}.garment-quote-download .button,.garment-quote-actions .button{white-space:normal;text-align:center}.garment-quote-actions{align-items:stretch}@media(max-width:600px){.garment-quote-layers{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}.garment-quote-actions .button{width:100%;box-sizing:border-box}}.article-main{min-width:0}.article-main table{min-width:700px}.article-main th[scope="row"]{width:24%;vertical-align:top}.article-main td{vertical-align:top;min-width:100px}.article-main td:last-child{min-width:220px}.article-main li{margin:0 0 10px}h2[id]{scroll-margin-top:120px}</style>
